  "summary": "Large biobank metabolomics and transcriptome QTL resources now enable direct linkage of metabolic traits to genetic and disease evidence.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is integration of metabolomic phenotypes with genetic association and clinical data. MetabHub mines UK Biobank plasma NMR metabolomics for mediation pathways, disease prediction and risk stratification. MetabDB integrates 16 public metabolomics studies into a searchable resource linking metabolic measures, QTLs, GWAS traits, diseases and genetic evidence. Related work extends genetic resolution: a Qatar Biobank transcriptome QTL catalog of about 7 million associations in 1,882 participants reports 1,379 novel eGenes and population-specific causal variants, and a heritability analysis of seven traits in 198,931 diverse individuals finds that rare and non-coding variants contribute substantially. What is new is resource-scale linkage of metabolic measures to genetic and clinical evidence, alongside population-specific genetic resolution.",
